This is where&nbsp; your work makes a difference. 

At Baxter, we believe every person-regardless of who they are or where they are from-deserves a chance to live a healthy life. It was our founding belief in 1931 and continues to be our guiding principle. We are redefining healthcare delivery to make a greater impact today, tomorrow, and beyond. 

Our Baxter colleagues are united by our Mission to Save and Sustain Lives. Together, our community is driven by a culture of courage, trust, and collaboration. Every individual is empowered to take ownership and make a meaningful impact. We strive for efficient and effective operations, and we hold each other accountable for delivering exceptional results. 

Here, you will find more than just a job-you will find purpose and pride. &nbsp; 

Your Role at Baxter

Apply a solid understanding of System Engineering practices and theories/practices in Risk Management toward the development of new or enhanced Software products or processes. Support the advancement of Risk and Reliability competencies and execution across the Device Systems Software Engineering organization. 

What you'll be doing: 

We are looking for a highly skilled Software Engineer who is comfortable with both front and back end programming. Full stack developers are responsible for developing and designing front end web architecture, ensuring the responsiveness of applications, and collaborating with UI/UX team. 

What you'll bring

- B. E. /B. Tech. in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Software Engineering or related field. 
 - 5-9 years experience. &nbsp; 
 - Knowledge of front-end technologies including VueJS, CSS3, JavaScript, and HTML5&nbsp; 
 - Understanding of object-oriented PHP programming. &nbsp; 
 - Experience with Docker , Helm Charts, Container , Cloud Computing&nbsp; 
 - Experience with C#, . NET Core - API Development, Performance improvement. &nbsp; 
 - Strong in PostgreSQL Database performance analysis and SQL/ PostgreSQL performance tuning&nbsp; 
 - Good to have MongoDB, Redis Cache, Devops knowledge&nbsp; 
 - Good to have Unix Scripting knowledge, MQTT, Keycloak&nbsp; 
 - A solid technical understanding of the principles and procedures of software engineering (e. g. , SDLC, IEC 62304, CMMI, Agile)&nbsp; 
 - Experience with software application architecture design and optimization&nbsp; 
 - Be passionate about software quality and be prepared to advocate on behalf of good processes and best practices. &nbsp; 
 - Ability to discuss normally encountered technical or project management issues, both verbally and in written form&nbsp; 
 - Experience with medical device or other regulated software engineering disciplines (e. g. , software development environments, configuration management tools, code inspection techniques and tools, testing methods and test management tools). &nbsp; 

Equal Employment Opportunity

Baxter is an equal opportunity employer. Baxter evaluates qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, gender, national origin, age, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, protected veteran status, disability/handicap status or any other legally protected characteristic. 

Reasonable Accommodations

Baxter is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodations to individuals with disabilities globally. If, because of a medical condition or disability, you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or interview process, please click on the link here and let us know the nature of your request along with your contact information. 

Recruitment Fraud Notice

Baxter has discovered incidents of employment scams, where fraudulent parties pose as Baxter employees, recruiters, or other agents, and engage with online job seekers in an attempt to steal personal and/or financial information. To learn how you can protect yourself, review our Recruitment Fraud Notice.

Hello, our name is Customertimes, but you can call us CT. We are a global digital engineering, product development, and technology consulting company. Headquartered in New York, we have a team of 1000+ experts working across 65+ countries. 

About the project: 

Join a Scrum team developing a global business intelligence and analytics platform used by pharmaceutical and life sciences companies to analyze commercial market data. You'll work across the full application stack, from the user interface down to the data layer, on a product that processes large volumes of healthcare data. 

Location: India (Remote)

How you'll make an impact: 

- Design, develop, and maintain features across the UI, business, and data layers of a . NET web application; 
 - Build and optimize data access and queries against Snowflake and other SQL databases; support data analysis and data management tasks; 
 - Deploy and support C# services on Linux in AWS; 
 - Take ownership of complex technical issues, work through them independently, and know when to bring in the team; 
 - Take part in all Scrum ceremonies (planning, daily stand-ups, reviews, and retrospectives) and support and mentor mid-level developers. What makes you a great fit: 

- 8+ years of professional full-stack development with C# and . NET on Windows; 
 - Hands-on experience across UI, business logic, and data layers in web applications; 
 - Strong SQL skills; experience with Snowflake or a similar SQL-based database engine; 
 - Experience deploying . NET/C# applications to AWS on Linux; 
 - Proven experience working in a Scrum team; 
 - Strong problem-solving skills and clear communication in English; 
 - Availability until at least 10: 30 AM EST (17: 30 Kyiv / 16: 30 CET) on business days. You are a star if you have: 

- Experience with the IQVIA FlexView codebase, or with pharma commercial data or BI/analytics platforms; 
 - AI-assisted development with Cursor (or similar tools) in C#; 
 - Experience with containers (Docker), CI/CD pipelines, and the migration of . NET Framework applications to modern . NET.

Line of Service
Advisory

Industry/Sector
Not Applicable

Specialism
Data, Analytics & AI

Management Level
